cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use camsim in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "camsim: deterministic camera sensor, ISP, and image-quality simulation"
abstract: >-
  camsim is a deterministic Python library that simulates a camera from spectral
  scene irradiance through a lens and sensor model to a RAW frame, processes the
  RAW frame through a modular image signal processor, and measures image quality
  with standard metrics. This 0.1.0 candidate validates the scene/optics helpers,
  sensor, ISP, metrics, camera orchestration, IO, and CLI. It is a simulated,
  EMVA 1288-style and ISO 12233-style validation, not a certified measurement of
  physical hardware. Machine-vision experiments are gated behind the G5 human
  sign-off and are not included; the candidate is not tagged or published until
  that approval is recorded.
version: 0.1.0.dev0
# date-released is intentionally omitted: this is a pre-sign-off G5 candidate,
# not a tagged release. Set it to the v0.1.0 tag date after the owner approves.
authors:
